WEBVTT

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:06.261
...so Harry throws it
in gear, floors the gas

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:08.933
and backs us right through
a burrito stand.

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.705
So when are you going
to teach me how to drive?

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.302
You sure you're ready?

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.075
I've piloted starships.

00:00:15.148 --> 00:00:17.116
I think I can handle a car.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.912
Ah, you'd be surprised.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:22.477
The clutch on a '69 Mustang
can be pretty tricky.

00:00:22.555 --> 00:00:23.544
Take a look.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.955
She's watching us again.

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:27.323
She's working.

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:28.884
Relax.

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.827
Dessert?

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.421
What is it?

00:00:32.499 --> 00:00:35.229
Some cheese I prepared
for our Kadi guest.

00:00:35.301 --> 00:00:36.734
Tell me what you think.

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:44.071
It's a little bland.

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.236
Just a little?

00:00:45.311 --> 00:00:46.573
Oh, that's bad.

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:48.238
The Kadi don't approve
of spices...

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.111
anything that might
inflame the senses.

00:00:50.183 --> 00:00:52.481
You're talking this mission
very seriously.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:53.985
The Kadi are easily offended.

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:56.113
The Captain's leaving
their representative

00:00:56.189 --> 00:00:58.521
entirely in my hands
while she's at the colony.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:00.855
I'm sure you're up to it,
Ambassador.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:02.258
I hope so.

00:01:04.264 --> 00:01:06.596
She's watching us again.

00:01:06.666 --> 00:01:08.634
You're imagining things.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.328
I don't think so.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:11.927
B'Elanna.

00:01:14.274 --> 00:01:15.935
Enjoying the view?

00:01:16.009 --> 00:01:17.271
Explain.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.368
You've been staring
at us all night.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:22.244
In fact,
you were following us yesterday

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:23.839
when we were walking
to Engineering,

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:25.043
and the day before,

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.313
when I was waiting for Tom
outside the Shuttle Bay.

00:01:27.387 --> 00:01:28.547
You are correct.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:32.284
I have been observing you
as part of my research

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.326
on human mating behavior.

00:01:36.062 --> 00:01:38.963
"Stardate 52647, 1400 hours.

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:44.093
"Subjects quarrel in corridor
outside female's quarters.

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:47.230
"Male returns with 12
flowering plant stems...

00:01:47.307 --> 00:01:48.899
"species Rosa rubifolia...

00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:51.569
"effecting a cessation
of hostilities.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:56.980
Stardate 526480300 hours.
Intimate relations resume..."

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.414
How the hell do you know

00:01:58.485 --> 00:02:00.385
when we're having
intimate relations?

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:02.216
There is no one
on Deck 9, Section 12

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.756
who doesn't know when you're
having intimate relations.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:05.756
Is there a problem?

00:02:05.825 --> 00:02:07.554
I want all the data
you've collected.

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.652
I haven't completed the study.

00:02:09.729 --> 00:02:10.889
Then study this...

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:12.522
Borg provokes Klingon.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.396
Klingon breaks Borg nose.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.297
B'Elanna...

00:02:15.368 --> 00:02:16.630
Call Sick Bay.

00:02:16.703 --> 00:02:19.035
Tell them there's about
to be a medical emergency.

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:20.333
B'Elanna, let's go
have a nightcap.

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.668
This time,
you've crossed the line.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:18.753
I've read B'Elanna's report.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.622
Needless to say,
I was surprised.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.854
I was careful
not to violate protocols.

00:04:22.929 --> 00:04:24.055
That's not the point.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:26.325
This is a starship,
not a nature preserve.

00:04:27.667 --> 00:04:29.396
Oh, I'm missing a pip.

00:04:29.469 --> 00:04:32.529
You asked me to broaden
my knowledge of human behavior.

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:33.936
I'm not questioning your goals,
Seven...

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:34.939
Oh.

00:04:35.008 --> 00:04:35.940
It's your methods.

00:04:36.009 --> 00:04:37.840
You shouldn't be taking
field notes on the crew.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.878
Help me with this,
will you, please?

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:44.449
Have you ever considered
trying it yourself?

00:04:44.517 --> 00:04:46.849
Romance, I mean.

00:04:46.919 --> 00:04:50.753
I do not require
a romantic relationship.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.189
So why did you collect
30,000 gigaquads

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:54.920
of data on the subject?

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.757
I'm late.

00:04:59.799 --> 00:05:02.290
I missed this on my first pass
through their database.

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.359
Kadi monks only wash
with purified water,

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:05.631
so sonic showers are out.

00:05:05.705 --> 00:05:07.172
I've already
equipped his quarters

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:10.175
with an ablutionary fountain
built to their specifications.

00:05:10.243 --> 00:05:11.710
They observe
eight daily services.

00:05:11.778 --> 00:05:13.143
Noted.

00:05:13.212 --> 00:05:14.577
Show the ambassador
our best side, Neelix.

00:05:14.647 --> 00:05:16.114
I don't want him going
back to his superiors

00:05:16.182 --> 00:05:18.150
with tales
of how immoral we are.

00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:21.418
Energize.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.259
The ritual greeting.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.660
Travelers who have left
the sanctity

00:05:36.736 --> 00:05:38.931
of their home and family,

00:05:39.005 --> 00:05:40.836
we welcome you into our home...

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:42.772
our family.

00:05:42.842 --> 00:05:45.743
Accept these symbols
of our purity

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.575
and the Goddess
Mother's blessing.

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.111
Commander Tuvok,
the senior officer

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:58.782
who will accompany me,

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.951
and Mr. Neelix, who will
familiarize your ambassador

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.049
with Voyager.

00:06:02.128 --> 00:06:06.189
Tomin is an excellent
judge of character.

00:06:06.265 --> 00:06:08.062
He'll help us determine
whether your crew is worthy

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:10.398
of receiving our minerals.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.301
He's in very good hands.

00:06:12.372 --> 00:06:15.637
It is time to welcome you
to our home.

00:06:31.591 --> 00:06:33.525
This way, Ambassador.

00:06:38.297 --> 00:06:40.561
Voyager's an Intrepid-class
starship

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:41.759
with a crew of 146,

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:43.893
designed
for long-term exploration.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:47.371
I thought we'd start with a tour
of our primary systems.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:48.930
First stop... Engineering.

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:50.669
I was hoping I might sample

00:06:50.743 --> 00:06:53.906
a food item I noted earlier
in your data files.

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:55.572
"Hasperat"?

00:06:55.648 --> 00:06:57.513
It's a Bajoran dish.

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:58.948
Very spicy.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:01.885
I believe that your dietary
protocols prohibit

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.581
flavorful foods.

00:07:03.656 --> 00:07:06.352
I want to broaden
my palate while I'm here

00:07:06.426 --> 00:07:09.020
in the interests
of better understanding.

00:07:09.095 --> 00:07:12.462
In that case,
first stop... Mess Hall.

00:07:14.434 --> 00:07:16.595
Your cortical implants
are operating

00:07:16.669 --> 00:07:17.795
at peak efficiency.

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.303
Nanoprobe levels stable.

00:07:19.372 --> 00:07:20.634
Complaints?

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:21.900
None.

00:07:22.041 --> 00:07:24.373
I heard about
the Mess Hall incident.

00:07:24.444 --> 00:07:28.244
This crew can be very efficient
at disseminating information

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.804
when they choose to be.

00:07:29.882 --> 00:07:33.374
They say gossip travels
faster than warp speed.

00:07:33.453 --> 00:07:35.580
So why were you studying
Tom and B'Elanna?

00:07:35.655 --> 00:07:38.089
Scientific curiosity.

00:07:38.157 --> 00:07:39.852
Are you sure?

00:07:39.926 --> 00:07:43.885
Perhaps there's a reason
that hasn't occurred to you.

00:07:43.963 --> 00:07:45.692
You're a woman, Seven.

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:48.495
Is that an observation
or a diagnosis?

00:07:48.568 --> 00:07:50.195
A simple biological fact...

00:07:50.269 --> 00:07:52.863
with repercussions
that are hard to deny.

00:07:52.939 --> 00:07:55.430
What is your proposed treatment?

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.408
Perhaps you should consider

00:07:57.477 --> 00:08:00.344
expanding your research
to the realm of dating.

00:08:00.413 --> 00:08:01.675
"Dating."

00:08:01.747 --> 00:08:03.408
You mean procreation.

00:08:03.483 --> 00:08:04.507
One step at a time.

00:08:04.584 --> 00:08:05.881
Dating is a human ritual

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:08.384
wherein two people share
a social activity...

00:08:08.454 --> 00:08:09.751
get to know each other.

00:08:09.822 --> 00:08:12.416
In time, it can lead
to a romantic involvement

00:08:12.492 --> 00:08:15.620
and eventually, if all
goes well, even marriage.

00:08:15.695 --> 00:08:17.458
One step at a time.

00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:21.364
This could be an important stage
in your social development.

00:08:21.434 --> 00:08:22.765
It's worth exploring.

00:08:22.835 --> 00:08:26.134
The Captain would seem to agree.

00:08:26.205 --> 00:08:28.332
How shall I proceed?

00:08:28.407 --> 00:08:29.806
You mean, we.

00:08:29.876 --> 00:08:31.070
I'll prepare a lesson plan.

00:08:31.143 --> 00:08:32.701
Meet me on Holodeck 2
in one hour.

00:08:32.778 --> 00:08:35.144
Most women start dating
a little younger than you,

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:36.476
but better late than never.

00:08:43.422 --> 00:08:46.050
I've prepared an introduction.

00:08:46.125 --> 00:08:49.322
I call it
"Love Amid the Stars."

00:08:51.264 --> 00:08:53.596
The Milky Way.

00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:55.634
Home to thousands
of humanoid species

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:59.102
and countless courtship rituals.

00:08:59.171 --> 00:09:04.074
Klingon males initiate courtship
by biting the female.

00:09:05.378 --> 00:09:08.575
Here we see two Bolians
getting to know one another.

00:09:08.648 --> 00:09:09.979
The courtship rituals
of some species

00:09:10.049 --> 00:09:12.847
remain shrouded in mystery.

00:09:12.919 --> 00:09:15.353
For example, Species 8472

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:19.323
appears to have as many
as five sexes.

00:09:19.392 --> 00:09:21.587
Bystanders better
keep their distance.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:25.856
Of course, the species

00:09:25.932 --> 00:09:28.230
you're most likely
to interact with is human,

00:09:28.301 --> 00:09:31.099
so without further ado,
Lesson One..."First Contact."

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:32.262
There are any number of ways

00:09:32.338 --> 00:09:34.431
humans can meet
prospective mates.

00:09:34.507 --> 00:09:37.999
Here we see
the "chance encounter."

00:09:38.077 --> 00:09:42.309
Equally common is
the "formal introduction."

00:09:42.381 --> 00:09:44.508
When first contact
is successful,

00:09:44.584 --> 00:09:46.381
romance quickly ensues

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:48.420
and, in the happiest
of circumstances,

00:09:48.487 --> 00:09:49.920
procreation.

00:09:50.990 --> 00:09:52.924
Here we see how fortress ovum

00:09:53.059 --> 00:09:56.392
is besieged by countless
little warriors.

00:09:56.462 --> 00:09:58.123
Doctor, I am familiar

00:09:58.197 --> 00:10:00.722
with the physiological processes
of sexuality.

00:10:02.201 --> 00:10:03.463
Well...

00:10:03.536 --> 00:10:04.935
then let's skip ahead

00:10:05.071 --> 00:10:07.904
to the first
of the practical exercises.

00:10:07.974 --> 00:10:11.034
Lesson Two...
"Encounter in a Public Place."

00:10:11.110 --> 00:10:15.171
Computer, initiate holo-program
Paris 3.

00:10:15.247 --> 00:10:17.044
Our location?

00:10:17.116 --> 00:10:19.084
Chez Sandrine.

00:10:19.151 --> 00:10:21.847
It's on Earth in a city
called Marseilles.

00:10:21.921 --> 00:10:24.446
Ensign Paris whiled
away a good portion

00:10:24.523 --> 00:10:26.150
of his Academy years here...

00:10:26.225 --> 00:10:29.786
no doubt to the detriment
of his scholastic performance.

00:10:29.862 --> 00:10:31.489
Now, pull up a bar stool

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:36.661
and pretend you've come here
to meet the man of your dreams.

00:10:39.538 --> 00:10:41.199
"Hi, there."

00:10:41.273 --> 00:10:42.535
"Hello."

00:10:42.608 --> 00:10:44.473
"Come here often?"

00:10:44.543 --> 00:10:46.340
"This is my first time."

00:10:46.412 --> 00:10:47.709
"You must be new in town.

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:49.611
How do you like
the south of France?"

00:10:49.682 --> 00:10:51.081
"It is very quaint...

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:53.641
exactly as I've
always pictured it."

00:10:53.719 --> 00:10:55.380
"May I buy you a drink?"

00:10:55.454 --> 00:10:57.854
I don't require
a liquid supplement

00:10:57.923 --> 00:10:58.855
at this time.

00:10:58.924 --> 00:11:00.721
You're not giving this
a fair chance.

00:11:00.793 --> 00:11:02.590
This exercise is pointless.

00:11:02.662 --> 00:11:03.686
It may seem pointless,

00:11:03.763 --> 00:11:05.628
but small talk is
a vital dating skill.

00:11:05.698 --> 00:11:08.690
It helps to establish
a rapport with your companion.

00:11:08.768 --> 00:11:10.827
Perhaps there's
something to be said

00:11:10.903 --> 00:11:12.666
for assimilation after all.

00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:16.265
All right. Why don't you
try your own approach on...

00:11:16.342 --> 00:11:18.173
that gentleman over there.

00:11:19.945 --> 00:11:22.106
Go ahead.

00:11:22.181 --> 00:11:23.910
Very well.

00:11:30.523 --> 00:11:33.959
- Hello.
- Hello.

00:11:34.093 --> 00:11:35.355
May I buy you a drink?

00:11:35.428 --> 00:11:38.488
Uh... sure.

00:11:38.564 --> 00:11:40.191
Steven Price.

00:11:43.469 --> 00:11:45.960
And... and you are?

00:11:46.072 --> 00:11:49.064
Seven of Nine,
Tertiary Adjunct of...

00:11:49.141 --> 00:11:50.733
You may call me Seven.

00:11:50.810 --> 00:11:54.246
Seven... that's-that's
an unusual name.

00:11:54.313 --> 00:11:56.907
Uh, please, have a seat.

00:12:06.158 --> 00:12:09.286
Looks like Sandrine's
is under new management.

00:12:09.361 --> 00:12:11.090
Who deleted my pool table?

00:12:11.163 --> 00:12:13.529
Shh. School is in session.

00:12:13.599 --> 00:12:15.362
More social lessons?

00:12:15.434 --> 00:12:18.335
Watch.
You might learn something.

00:12:20.573 --> 00:12:21.801
Curious jewelry.

00:12:21.874 --> 00:12:23.432
It's a Borg implant.

00:12:23.509 --> 00:12:24.601
I was a drone.

00:12:24.677 --> 00:12:26.508
Oh, so then it's
a family heirloom.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.047
Borg do not have families.

00:12:29.115 --> 00:12:30.343
They have unimatrices.

00:12:30.416 --> 00:12:33.385
Well, in that case,
why don't you tell me

00:12:33.452 --> 00:12:35.249
about your... Unimatrix.

00:12:35.321 --> 00:12:37.653
They're hitting it off,
don't you think?

00:12:37.723 --> 00:12:39.054
He's a hologram.

00:12:39.125 --> 00:12:40.524
Your point?

00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:43.528
Well, you programmed him
to interact with Seven.

00:12:43.596 --> 00:12:45.962
Real people don't
respond the same way.

00:12:46.031 --> 00:12:48.090
Under my guidance,
she'll be dating real people

00:12:48.167 --> 00:12:50.101
in no time.

00:12:50.169 --> 00:12:52.694
You're teaching
Seven how to date?

00:12:54.106 --> 00:12:56.939
Talk about the blind
leading the blind.

00:12:57.009 --> 00:12:59.739
I've had my share
of romantic encounters.

00:12:59.812 --> 00:13:01.473
Hmm.

00:13:01.547 --> 00:13:04.209
Are you implying
that Seven couldn't get a date?

00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:05.545
What, are you kidding?

00:13:05.618 --> 00:13:07.813
Half the men on this ship
would jump at the chance.

00:13:07.887 --> 00:13:09.479
But getting a date is one thing.

00:13:09.555 --> 00:13:11.785
Keeping it from turning
into a disaster is another.

00:13:11.857 --> 00:13:15.224
I have every confidence
in her social skills.

00:13:17.496 --> 00:13:18.758
Well, fine.

00:13:18.831 --> 00:13:20.321
Let's say you get her a date.

00:13:20.399 --> 00:13:21.491
This is the holodeck.

00:13:21.567 --> 00:13:23.398
The cards are stacked
in her favor.

00:13:23.469 --> 00:13:25.869
But if you want to really
put her to the test,

00:13:25.938 --> 00:13:27.769
you have to do it
in the real world,

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:29.239
where anything can happen.

00:13:30.743 --> 00:13:32.608
Mr. Neelix is hosting
a reception

00:13:32.678 --> 00:13:35.112
for the Kadi Ambassador
on Thursday night.

00:13:35.181 --> 00:13:37.376
Not only will Seven arrive
with a date,

00:13:37.449 --> 00:13:40.577
she will have him eating
out of the palm of her hand.

00:13:40.653 --> 00:13:42.780
Put your latinum
where your mouth is.

00:13:42.855 --> 00:13:45.119
If Seven brings a date
to the reception

00:13:45.191 --> 00:13:47.751
and leaves with the same date
on good terms

00:13:47.827 --> 00:13:49.954
without causing
a diplomatic incident,

00:13:50.029 --> 00:13:53.430
I will work double shifts
in Sick Bay for the next month.

00:13:53.499 --> 00:13:54.966
And if she fails?

00:13:55.067 --> 00:13:56.398
I get a month off.

00:13:56.468 --> 00:13:58.095
It's a bet.

00:14:01.707 --> 00:14:03.834
Where are you going?

00:14:03.909 --> 00:14:05.900
Our small talk is terminated.

00:14:07.580 --> 00:14:09.514
I have mastered this exercise.

00:14:09.582 --> 00:14:11.345
We can proceed to the next.

00:14:11.417 --> 00:14:12.406
If I were you,

00:14:12.484 --> 00:14:15.612
I'd start looking for somebody
to fill in for me.

00:14:28.334 --> 00:14:30.529
One Katarian pudding.

00:14:31.804 --> 00:14:33.271
Mm-hmm.

00:14:34.974 --> 00:14:36.066
Ah.

00:14:38.143 --> 00:14:40.577
Mmm!

00:14:40.646 --> 00:14:44.173
Ah, the texture is so frothy.

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:46.946
It seems to be evaporating
in my mouth.

00:14:47.019 --> 00:14:48.884
The recipe includes
a catalytic agent

00:14:48.954 --> 00:14:50.683
designed to do just that.

00:14:50.756 --> 00:14:52.280
Mmm.

00:14:52.358 --> 00:14:55.054
If we don't hurry,
we'll miss Lieutenant Torres.

00:14:55.127 --> 00:14:56.788
She's been waiting half an hour.

00:14:56.862 --> 00:14:57.954
You're right.

00:14:58.097 --> 00:15:00.759
Engineering.
Your warp core.

00:15:00.833 --> 00:15:02.994
I must see that.

00:15:06.972 --> 00:15:09.634
In our society, males
and females work separately.

00:15:09.708 --> 00:15:11.676
But I can see the wisdom
of your approach.

00:15:11.744 --> 00:15:16.681
Promotes a more stimulating
environment.

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:20.082
It's time for third prayer.

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:21.915
Yes, it is.

00:15:22.054 --> 00:15:24.215
But I think I can forego
this service

00:15:24.290 --> 00:15:26.815
and perform
the appropriate penance later.

00:15:26.892 --> 00:15:29.452
It's more important

00:15:29.528 --> 00:15:34.090
that I continue exploring
your culture.

00:15:34.166 --> 00:15:35.326
Perhaps another dessert.

00:15:38.070 --> 00:15:39.469
Good morning.

00:15:39.538 --> 00:15:42.166
It's time for Lesson Three...

00:15:42.241 --> 00:15:43.640
"Getting to Know You."

00:15:43.709 --> 00:15:44.733
Elaborate.

00:15:44.810 --> 00:15:47.142
The key to finding
a compatible partner

00:15:47.212 --> 00:15:50.306
is learning how to share
your interests and goals.

00:15:50.382 --> 00:15:52.213
We'll start with hobbies.

00:15:52.284 --> 00:15:54.548
What do you do
with your spare time?

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:56.485
Regenerate.

00:15:56.555 --> 00:15:57.783
Uh-huh.

00:15:57.856 --> 00:16:00.950
Tell me about your tastes,
your likes and dislikes.

00:16:01.060 --> 00:16:03.153
I dislike irrelevant
conversations.

00:16:03.228 --> 00:16:06.129
Okay.
Which brings us to "goals."

00:16:06.198 --> 00:16:08.758
What do you want out of life?

00:16:08.834 --> 00:16:09.892
Perfection.

00:16:09.969 --> 00:16:12.233
Perfection is a laudable
goal for oneself,

00:16:12.304 --> 00:16:14.329
but you can't expect
it from others.

00:16:14.406 --> 00:16:17.534
I learned that lesson myself
when I was first activated.

00:16:17.609 --> 00:16:20.510
One of the ways
I adapted was to pursue

00:16:20.579 --> 00:16:24.845
interests people
could identify with.

00:16:24.917 --> 00:16:26.282
Holo-photography, for example.

00:16:26.352 --> 00:16:27.580
Opera.

00:16:27.653 --> 00:16:30.178
Music does have intriguing
mathematical properties.

00:16:30.255 --> 00:16:31.517
Excellent.

00:16:31.590 --> 00:16:33.182
Perhaps we can
mold this curiosity

00:16:33.258 --> 00:16:34.190
into an interest...

00:16:34.259 --> 00:16:36.557
something you can
share with others.

00:16:36.628 --> 00:16:39.392
Let's see how much you know.

00:16:40.799 --> 00:16:42.892
Here we see...

00:16:42.968 --> 00:16:45.732
A basic musical phrase
in the major mode.

00:16:45.804 --> 00:16:49.035
I've done a preliminary study
of the topic.

00:16:49.108 --> 00:16:51.372
Sing it for me.

00:16:53.245 --> 00:16:58.740
La-la-la-la-la-la-la-la-la.

00:16:58.817 --> 00:17:03.880
Seven, has anyone ever told you
you have a beautiful voice?

00:17:03.956 --> 00:17:04.888
It's a true gift.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.582
The gift is
from the collective...

00:17:06.658 --> 00:17:08.853
a vocal subprocessor
designed to facilitate

00:17:08.927 --> 00:17:11.122
the sonic interface
with Borg transponders.

00:17:11.196 --> 00:17:14.597
Let's try something
a little more challenging.

00:17:14.666 --> 00:17:17.658
"You Are My Sunshine."

00:17:17.736 --> 00:17:19.897
It's a simple melody
from Earth's 20th century.

00:17:19.972 --> 00:17:21.735
A good piece for beginners.

00:17:21.807 --> 00:17:23.240
Sing.

00:17:24.843 --> 00:17:30.611
The other night, dear,
as I lay sleeping

00:17:30.682 --> 00:17:35.016
I dreamed I held you
in my arms.

00:17:35.087 --> 00:17:37.317
That was... flawless,

00:17:37.389 --> 00:17:40.324
but try putting a little
more emotion into it.

00:17:40.392 --> 00:17:41.450
Like this.

00:17:43.295 --> 00:17:49.564
When I awoke, dear,
I was mistaken

00:17:49.635 --> 00:17:56.165
And I hung my head and cried.

00:17:56.241 --> 00:18:00.769
See? Computer, add
instrumental accompaniment.

00:18:02.281 --> 00:18:04.112
On to the chorus.

00:18:04.183 --> 00:18:06.276
Together now.

00:18:06.351 --> 00:18:11.379
You are my sunshine,
my only sunshine

00:18:11.457 --> 00:18:16.656
You make me happy
when skies are gray

00:18:16.728 --> 00:18:21.893
You'll never know, dear,
how much I love you

00:18:22.034 --> 00:18:27.062
Please don't take
my sunshine away

00:18:27.139 --> 00:18:32.702
You are my sunshine,
my only sunshine

00:18:32.778 --> 00:18:37.511
You make me happy
when skies are gray

00:18:37.583 --> 00:18:38.845
You'll never know, dear

00:18:38.917 --> 00:18:42.853
How much I love you

00:18:42.921 --> 00:18:48.757
Please don't take
my sunshine away.

00:18:58.403 --> 00:18:59.631
Seven, I need the data

00:18:59.705 --> 00:19:01.866
from those last two
astrometric scans.

00:19:01.940 --> 00:19:02.872
In a moment.

00:19:03.008 --> 00:19:05.772
That looks
like the crew manifest.

00:19:05.844 --> 00:19:08.745
The Doctor asked me to pick
a suitable candidate.

00:19:08.814 --> 00:19:09.746
For what?

00:19:09.815 --> 00:19:13.046
Lesson Ten..."The First Date."

00:19:13.118 --> 00:19:16.144
Your... first date?

00:19:16.221 --> 00:19:17.620
I've narrowed the list
to two crewmen

00:19:17.689 --> 00:19:19.850
based on work performance
and compatible interests.

00:19:19.925 --> 00:19:22.257
I didn't know you had
any interests.

00:19:22.327 --> 00:19:23.817
Neither did I,

00:19:23.896 --> 00:19:27.491
but, apparently, they include
astronomy, quantum mechanics

00:19:27.566 --> 00:19:28.533
and music.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:30.397
I play the clarinet, you know.

00:19:30.469 --> 00:19:33.870
You are not one
of the candidates, Ensign.

00:19:33.939 --> 00:19:35.270
Oh.

00:19:36.341 --> 00:19:40.801
Well, maybe I can help
you pick Mr. Right.

00:19:40.879 --> 00:19:44.542
Ensign Bronowsky,
assigned to the Airponics Bay.

00:19:44.616 --> 00:19:46.550
His work record is flawless
and he plays the accordion.

00:19:46.618 --> 00:19:47.915
Badly, very badly.

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:49.453
He's got no sense of humor.

00:19:51.823 --> 00:19:54.519
Lieutenant Chapman,
Structural Engineering.

00:19:54.593 --> 00:19:56.458
Chapman's a nice guy.

00:19:56.528 --> 00:19:59.122
We worked together
on an away mission.

00:19:59.198 --> 00:20:01.257
He seemed efficient.

00:20:05.237 --> 00:20:07.933
Robertson, if that's you,
I need an isolinear spanner.

00:20:08.006 --> 00:20:08.938
It is not.

00:20:09.041 --> 00:20:10.668
Ooh.

00:20:11.743 --> 00:20:12.937
I apologize, Lieutenant.

00:20:13.078 --> 00:20:14.636
I didn't mean to startle you.

00:20:14.713 --> 00:20:16.146
No, my fault.

00:20:16.215 --> 00:20:18.410
You need something?

00:20:18.483 --> 00:20:19.950
Your presence is required...

00:20:20.052 --> 00:20:22.782
...er, rather, it is
requested tonight.

00:20:22.854 --> 00:20:24.788
1900 hours, Holodeck 2.

00:20:24.856 --> 00:20:26.915
Another Engineering simulation?

00:20:26.992 --> 00:20:28.482
Dinner.

00:20:28.560 --> 00:20:30.289
"Dinner"?

00:20:30.362 --> 00:20:32.694
The consumption
of nutritional biomatter.

00:20:32.764 --> 00:20:34.959
No, I know what dinner is.

00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:37.967
I just...

00:20:38.070 --> 00:20:40.937
Are you asking me to join you?

00:20:41.006 --> 00:20:42.439
Yes.

00:20:44.776 --> 00:20:45.970
State your response.

00:20:46.111 --> 00:20:48.671
Okay.

00:20:48.747 --> 00:20:50.374
Yes.

00:20:50.449 --> 00:20:52.110
Please be punctual.

00:20:52.184 --> 00:20:54.209
I will. Thanks.

00:20:54.286 --> 00:20:56.880
A dropped tool can be
a workplace hazard.

00:20:56.955 --> 00:20:58.479
Be more careful next time.

00:21:01.460 --> 00:21:04.554
Seven, please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:21:04.630 --> 00:21:05.927
I have a date.

00:21:20.178 --> 00:21:21.304
Sorry I'm late.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:22.540
It's quite all right.

00:21:22.614 --> 00:21:25.378
In fact, why don't you
take the day off...

00:21:25.450 --> 00:21:26.382
relax?

00:21:26.451 --> 00:21:28.214
Those double shifts
are going to take

00:21:28.287 --> 00:21:29.049
a lot out of you.

00:21:29.121 --> 00:21:30.053
Oh?

00:21:30.122 --> 00:21:32.147
Seven of Nine has
a date tonight.

00:21:32.224 --> 00:21:33.851
If all goes well,
as I'm sure it will,

00:21:33.925 --> 00:21:36.655
he'll accompany her
to the reception tomorrow.

00:21:36.728 --> 00:21:39.060
Who'd she pick?

00:21:39.131 --> 00:21:40.655
Lieutenant William Chapman.

00:21:41.733 --> 00:21:42.665
Chapman!

00:21:42.734 --> 00:21:43.666
Good luck.

00:21:43.735 --> 00:21:45.100
What's that supposed to mean?

00:21:45.170 --> 00:21:47.434
He's renowned
for being nervous around women.

00:21:47.506 --> 00:21:48.473
So?

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:49.632
Are you kidding?

00:21:49.708 --> 00:21:51.073
Seven's dominant personality

00:21:51.143 --> 00:21:52.974
will have him running
for the airlock

00:21:53.045 --> 00:21:53.977
before dessert.

00:21:54.046 --> 00:21:55.536
Seven may seem intimidating,

00:21:55.614 --> 00:21:58.811
but that's only a reaction
to the way people treat her.

00:21:58.884 --> 00:22:00.647
In fact, she's...

00:22:00.719 --> 00:22:03.313
an efficient
and charming young woman.

00:22:03.388 --> 00:22:05.322
Efficient...
I'll give you that...

00:22:05.390 --> 00:22:06.652
but charming?

00:22:06.725 --> 00:22:08.920
Most people don't
take the time to look

00:22:08.994 --> 00:22:10.188
beyond her exterior.

00:22:10.262 --> 00:22:12.924
Did you know she has
a lovely singing voice?

00:22:13.065 --> 00:22:15.533
Uh, no, I didn't,
but then again,

00:22:15.600 --> 00:22:17.659
I've never asked her
to sing for me.

00:22:17.736 --> 00:22:18.930
What are you implying?

00:22:19.071 --> 00:22:21.130
Well, it sounds like
you're getting

00:22:21.206 --> 00:22:23.606
a little infatuated
with your star pupil.

00:22:24.676 --> 00:22:25.643
"Infatuated"?

00:22:25.711 --> 00:22:26.939
That's absurd.

00:22:27.045 --> 00:22:28.945
Whatever you say, maestro.

00:22:29.081 --> 00:22:31.982
It was part
of the lesson plan!

00:22:42.027 --> 00:22:44.325
You're meeting with him
in ten minutes, Seven.

00:22:44.396 --> 00:22:45.488
Why aren't you ready?

00:22:45.564 --> 00:22:46.531
I am.

00:22:46.598 --> 00:22:48.065
Aren't we forgetting something?

00:22:48.133 --> 00:22:50.966
Lesson Eight...
"Dress for Success."

00:22:51.036 --> 00:22:52.697
My appearance is sufficient.

00:22:52.771 --> 00:22:53.897
Sufficient, yes,

00:22:53.972 --> 00:22:56.600
but you could use
a little more... panache.

00:22:56.675 --> 00:22:59.143
Let's start by doing
something different

00:22:59.211 --> 00:23:00.473
with your hair.

00:23:00.545 --> 00:23:02.911
I don't have much
first-hand experience

00:23:03.048 --> 00:23:04.515
with this, but, uh...

00:23:07.719 --> 00:23:08.913
try...

00:23:09.054 --> 00:23:10.885
shaking your head a little bit.

00:23:13.225 --> 00:23:15.159
Is this more appropriate?

00:23:16.728 --> 00:23:17.820
Yes.

00:23:17.896 --> 00:23:21.388
When I first designed
your dermaplastic garment,

00:23:21.466 --> 00:23:24.663
I also tried my hand
at some casual attire.

00:23:24.736 --> 00:23:27.500
You might want
to replicate one of these.

00:23:27.572 --> 00:23:28.937
How shall I choose?

00:23:29.074 --> 00:23:31.338
I think you'd look
very nice in...

00:23:31.410 --> 00:23:33.674
this one.

00:23:33.745 --> 00:23:37.181
I am uncertain how to wear
such a garment.

00:23:37.249 --> 00:23:38.511
Assist me.

00:23:38.583 --> 00:23:40.312
Oh, I-I-I'm sure you'll manage.

00:23:40.385 --> 00:23:42.046
I'll go prepare the holodeck.

00:23:42.120 --> 00:23:44.554
Remember, the idea is
to have fun tonight.

00:23:44.623 --> 00:23:47.057
I'll expect a full report
in the morning.

00:24:15.220 --> 00:24:17.154
You-you look beautiful.

00:24:17.222 --> 00:24:18.154
Thank you.

00:24:18.223 --> 00:24:19.918
You look...

00:24:19.991 --> 00:24:22.653
beautiful as well.

00:24:22.727 --> 00:24:23.659
Thank you.

00:24:25.063 --> 00:24:27.361
Uh, would you like to sit down?

00:24:27.432 --> 00:24:29.525
Where is
our designated location?

00:24:29.601 --> 00:24:31.228
Best table in the house.

00:24:36.575 --> 00:24:38.668
I wasn't sure
you'd actually show up.

00:24:38.743 --> 00:24:40.267
I requested your presence.

00:24:40.345 --> 00:24:41.334
Well, to be honest,

00:24:41.413 --> 00:24:44.041
I thought one of my friends
put you up to it.

00:24:53.592 --> 00:24:55.150
Um... champagne?

00:24:55.227 --> 00:24:57.161
Synthehol impairs
my cortical function.

00:24:57.229 --> 00:24:58.196
Water will suffice.

00:24:58.263 --> 00:24:59.992
Mind if I...

00:25:01.066 --> 00:25:01.998
Proceed.

00:25:02.067 --> 00:25:05.093
I must admit
I'm a little nervous.

00:25:05.170 --> 00:25:06.034
Elaborate.

00:25:06.104 --> 00:25:08.629
Oh, um...

00:25:08.707 --> 00:25:11.403
let's just say it's
been a long time

00:25:11.476 --> 00:25:13.706
since I've been out on a date.

00:25:13.778 --> 00:25:15.302
I've never been on a date.

00:25:15.380 --> 00:25:18.816
As a result, I am experiencing
anxiety as well.

00:25:18.884 --> 00:25:22.047
Well, I guess that means
we've got something in common.

00:25:27.125 --> 00:25:28.422
Uh...

00:25:30.729 --> 00:25:31.787
Garcon?

00:25:34.032 --> 00:25:35.727
Server, report to this station.

00:25:35.800 --> 00:25:37.199
We require your assistance.

00:26:07.165 --> 00:26:08.257
Problem?

00:26:08.333 --> 00:26:11.268
This creature has
an exoskeleton.

00:26:11.336 --> 00:26:13.270
It's a lobster.

00:26:13.338 --> 00:26:15.898
They're a delicacy on Earth.

00:26:16.041 --> 00:26:17.338
Try it.

00:26:28.687 --> 00:26:32.020
I will replicate you
a new garment.

00:26:32.090 --> 00:26:33.352
I'm fine, fine.

00:26:33.425 --> 00:26:35.325
It's just a little bit of...

00:26:35.393 --> 00:26:36.485
exoskeleton.

00:26:37.729 --> 00:26:39.458
Maybe we should order dessert.

00:26:39.531 --> 00:26:42.227
You wish to accelerate
our social encounter?

00:26:42.300 --> 00:26:43.927
No, no. I didn't say that.

00:26:44.069 --> 00:26:45.832
I'm just, uh...

00:26:45.904 --> 00:26:49.340
I'm having a very...
interesting evening.

00:26:51.242 --> 00:26:52.971
W-would you like to dance?

00:26:54.045 --> 00:26:55.945
That activity is
covered in Lesson 35.

00:26:56.081 --> 00:26:57.378
I haven't reached it yet.

00:26:58.617 --> 00:27:00.881
Well, I'm not much
of a dancer myself...

00:27:00.952 --> 00:27:02.283
but it might be fun.

00:27:02.354 --> 00:27:04.117
As you wish.

00:27:13.632 --> 00:27:14.564
Oh...

00:27:15.634 --> 00:27:16.601
Relax.

00:27:24.542 --> 00:27:25.668
Try to relax.

00:27:25.744 --> 00:27:27.143
You seem a little tense.

00:27:27.212 --> 00:27:29.908
Relaxation would disrupt
my chronographic sequencer.

00:27:30.015 --> 00:27:32.415
It allows me to maintain
synchronous movement

00:27:32.484 --> 00:27:33.473
with the music.

00:27:33.551 --> 00:27:34.916
That's handy...

00:27:35.020 --> 00:27:38.820
but maybe you could ignore
your chronographic sequencer

00:27:38.890 --> 00:27:40.357
and, uh, let me lead.

00:27:46.731 --> 00:27:47.857
That's better.

00:28:07.719 --> 00:28:09.516
Oh!

00:28:10.922 --> 00:28:11.980
You are damaged.

00:28:12.057 --> 00:28:13.319
No...

00:28:13.391 --> 00:28:14.688
I'll be all right.

00:28:20.198 --> 00:28:21.597
You've torn a ligament.

00:28:21.666 --> 00:28:24.362
I'm afraid you'll have
to report to Sick Bay.

00:28:24.436 --> 00:28:25.903
Mr. Paris will treat you.

00:28:26.037 --> 00:28:28.301
No need to mention
how this happened.

00:28:31.710 --> 00:28:33.871
I had a great time, Seven.

00:28:33.945 --> 00:28:35.810
Let's do this again...

00:28:35.880 --> 00:28:37.074
s-someday.

00:28:41.052 --> 00:28:42.144
I have failed.

00:28:42.220 --> 00:28:43.482
Nonsense.

00:28:43.555 --> 00:28:46.547
Even Romeo and Juliet
hit a few snags at first.

00:28:46.624 --> 00:28:50.651
Besides, Lieutenant Chapman's
not the only lobster in the sea.

00:28:50.729 --> 00:28:52.924
I wish to terminate
our social lessons.

00:28:53.064 --> 00:28:55.931
Just because you didn't
achieve perfection

00:28:56.034 --> 00:28:59.595
your first time out
doesn't mean you should give up.

00:28:59.671 --> 00:29:01.866
Dating is a poor means
of interaction.

00:29:01.940 --> 00:29:03.532
There is far more efficiency

00:29:03.608 --> 00:29:05.508
in the way
you and I communicate.

00:29:05.577 --> 00:29:08.512
We say what we mean
simply and directly.

00:29:08.580 --> 00:29:12.846
You and I do have a rapport,
but we're colleagues.

00:29:12.917 --> 00:29:15.283
We're not pursuing romance.

00:29:15.353 --> 00:29:16.615
No.

00:29:16.688 --> 00:29:18.087
I'm certain you'll be able

00:29:18.156 --> 00:29:20.681
to master these basic
skills in short order.

00:29:20.759 --> 00:29:23.489
My first date was
certainly short.

00:29:24.863 --> 00:29:26.296
Was that a joke?

00:29:26.364 --> 00:29:28.525
Lesson Six..."Beguiling Banter."

00:29:28.600 --> 00:29:30.465
Now you're getting
the hang of it.

00:29:30.535 --> 00:29:33.402
Perhaps this evening doesn't
have to end so abruptly.

00:29:33.471 --> 00:29:34.699
This may be a good time

00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:36.741
to cover Lesson 35...
"Shall We Dance?"

00:29:36.808 --> 00:29:39.368
Computer, play "Someone
To Watch Over Me"

00:29:39.444 --> 00:29:40.706
instrumental only.

00:29:44.449 --> 00:29:47.043
We'll begin
with some simple steps.

00:29:47.118 --> 00:29:49.746
Place your left hand
on my shoulder

00:29:49.821 --> 00:29:52.153
and your right hand in my left.

00:29:52.223 --> 00:29:54.657
Now... follow me...

00:29:54.726 --> 00:29:56.523
one step at a time.

00:30:03.401 --> 00:30:06.529
Don't worry. I don't have
any ligaments to tear.

00:30:35.900 --> 00:30:37.333
Another drink!

00:30:41.272 --> 00:30:42.569
Ambassador!

00:30:42.640 --> 00:30:43.971
Neelix!

00:30:44.042 --> 00:30:47.239
My friend, my... host...

00:30:47.312 --> 00:30:49.371
my... savior.

00:30:49.447 --> 00:30:54.680
Neelix, I want you to meet,
uh...

00:30:54.752 --> 00:30:55.844
Alandra...

00:30:57.255 --> 00:30:59.553
and Tria.

00:30:59.624 --> 00:31:00.921
What are you doing?

00:31:00.992 --> 00:31:03.256
I'm sampling yet another entrée

00:31:03.328 --> 00:31:07.355
on the menu of pleasure
that you have opened up for me.

00:31:07.432 --> 00:31:09.332
I checked today's menu,
and they're not on it.

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:10.424
Coffee... black.

00:31:10.501 --> 00:31:13.026
Neelix, I decided
to go exploring

00:31:13.104 --> 00:31:15.402
and I found your holodecks...

00:31:15.473 --> 00:31:17.907
and I discovered this little gem

00:31:17.976 --> 00:31:20.877
still simmering
in the memory buffer.

00:31:20.945 --> 00:31:22.879
We can explore it later.
Right now, we've got to get you

00:31:22.947 --> 00:31:23.914
to your reception.

00:31:25.683 --> 00:31:27.207
Mmm... pungent taste.
What is it?

00:31:27.285 --> 00:31:28.343
Coffee

00:31:28.419 --> 00:31:30.319
and there's plenty more
where we're going.

00:31:30.388 --> 00:31:32.288
No coffee on our colony.

00:31:32.357 --> 00:31:34.689
Nothing to tempt the appetite

00:31:34.759 --> 00:31:38.058
of even the most
weak-willed novitiate.

00:31:38.129 --> 00:31:39.960
Neelix, a confession.

00:31:40.031 --> 00:31:43.159
I am thinking of
leaving the colony...

00:31:43.234 --> 00:31:44.599
joining Voyager.

00:31:44.669 --> 00:31:46.933
I want to throw off my vows

00:31:47.005 --> 00:31:50.907
and immerse myself
in your wonderful culture.

00:31:50.975 --> 00:31:52.966
That's just
the synthehol talking.

00:31:53.077 --> 00:31:58.606
No, I've never been more
clear-headed about anything.

00:31:58.683 --> 00:32:02.551
And I have you to thank.

00:32:02.620 --> 00:32:04.645
That's right...
there we go...

00:32:04.722 --> 00:32:06.986
It's all you...

00:32:09.928 --> 00:32:11.361
Hard at work?

00:32:11.429 --> 00:32:13.920
Our lessons
have disrupted my duties.

00:32:14.032 --> 00:32:15.431
Then I suppose you're too busy

00:32:15.500 --> 00:32:17.263
to attend
the Ambassador's reception.

00:32:17.335 --> 00:32:18.825
My presence is not required.

00:32:18.903 --> 00:32:21.463
True... but it might be
an opportunity for you

00:32:21.539 --> 00:32:23.564
to apply your newfound
social skills.

00:32:23.641 --> 00:32:25.336
Lesson 11...
"Life of the Party."

00:32:25.410 --> 00:32:27.139
Exactly. Join me?

00:32:27.211 --> 00:32:30.339
Are you asking me on a date?

00:32:31.416 --> 00:32:33.179
I suppose I am.

00:32:33.251 --> 00:32:34.343
Then I accept.

00:32:34.419 --> 00:32:36.649
Is my appearance sufficient?

00:32:36.721 --> 00:32:38.621
You look perfect.

00:32:45.396 --> 00:32:48.422
How do you bend
a hologram's ear?

00:32:48.499 --> 00:32:49.659
Use a prism.

00:32:51.803 --> 00:32:54.966
What did the counselor
say to the hologram?

00:32:55.073 --> 00:32:56.563
"You're projecting."

00:32:56.641 --> 00:32:59.838
This humor...
it's a revelation.

00:32:59.911 --> 00:33:00.935
Ambassador?

00:33:01.012 --> 00:33:01.944
Very good.

00:33:02.013 --> 00:33:03.173
Uh... are-are you sure

00:33:03.247 --> 00:33:05.613
you wouldn't prefer
some more coffee, Ambassador?

00:33:05.683 --> 00:33:08.049
Coffee. Mmm, yes.
I'll have that, too.

00:33:08.119 --> 00:33:09.086
Go.

00:33:12.757 --> 00:33:15.317
Neelix...
is it my imagination

00:33:15.393 --> 00:33:17.122
or is our guest of honor drunk?

00:33:17.195 --> 00:33:18.457
Commander, I tried.

00:33:18.529 --> 00:33:19.791
I had an itinerary.

00:33:19.864 --> 00:33:22.799
I even set up a prayer dais
in his quarters,

00:33:22.867 --> 00:33:25.062
but I just couldn't control him.

00:33:25.136 --> 00:33:26.694
The Captain is due
back in the morning

00:33:26.771 --> 00:33:27.760
with the Kadi Minister.

00:33:27.839 --> 00:33:28.931
What do I do?

00:33:29.073 --> 00:33:30.631
Pray.

00:33:38.282 --> 00:33:39.374
Well, well, well.

00:33:39.450 --> 00:33:40.815
What do we have here?

00:33:40.885 --> 00:33:43.183
Mr. Paris, I believe you know
Seven of Nine...

00:33:43.254 --> 00:33:44.516
my date for the evening.

00:33:44.589 --> 00:33:45.681
Oh, you don't say?

00:33:45.757 --> 00:33:48.351
Well, your last date
ended up in Sick Bay.

00:33:48.426 --> 00:33:50.894
I hope this one
goes a little smoother.

00:33:50.962 --> 00:33:53.157
There's no need to be insulting.

00:33:53.231 --> 00:33:54.220
It's all right, Doctor.

00:33:54.298 --> 00:33:56.425
I believe he is merely
engaging in small talk.

00:33:56.501 --> 00:33:58.469
May I get either
of you gentlemen a drink?

00:33:58.536 --> 00:34:00.868
Ah, yes, gin and tonic
with a twist.

00:34:00.938 --> 00:34:02.098
You know I don't drink.

00:34:02.173 --> 00:34:03.875
I don't have
the stomach for it.

00:34:03.941 --> 00:34:05.704
A well-crafted joke, Doctor.

00:34:10.681 --> 00:34:13.878
Impressive. You've actually
taught her to be polite.

00:34:13.951 --> 00:34:16.112
But don't think
you've won our bet.

00:34:16.187 --> 00:34:18.519
She was supposed
to bring a real date.

00:34:18.589 --> 00:34:20.682
Photons and force fields,
flesh and blood...

00:34:20.758 --> 00:34:22.089
why quibble over details?

00:34:22.160 --> 00:34:23.593
I'm just as real as any of you.

00:34:23.661 --> 00:34:25.754
Where is that funny man?

00:34:25.830 --> 00:34:29.425
Mr. Tomin, please,
why don't we sit down?

00:34:29.500 --> 00:34:31.593
Ah, there he is...
there he is.

00:34:31.669 --> 00:34:33.466
Ensign Paris, tell us

00:34:33.538 --> 00:34:36.473
another one of those
hologram jokes.

00:34:36.541 --> 00:34:38.270
You've been stealing
my material?

00:34:38.342 --> 00:34:41.175
That guy's so lubricated
he'll laugh at anything.

00:34:41.245 --> 00:34:42.212
There he is.

00:34:42.280 --> 00:34:44.373
The Ambassador of Humor.

00:34:46.350 --> 00:34:48.284
I could use a little help here.

00:34:48.352 --> 00:34:51.719
Seven, perhaps now
would be a good time

00:34:51.789 --> 00:34:55.247
to review Lesson 23...
"Toast of the Town."

00:34:55.326 --> 00:34:56.759
Very well.

00:35:00.798 --> 00:35:03.790
Ladies and gentlemen,
I require your attention.

00:35:03.868 --> 00:35:05.631
May cultural differences

00:35:05.703 --> 00:35:08.900
encourage us to build bridges
of understanding.

00:35:09.040 --> 00:35:11.133
To all that makes us unique.

00:35:19.183 --> 00:35:21.014
Who is
that extraordinary female?

00:35:21.085 --> 00:35:22.211
Seven of Nine.

00:35:22.286 --> 00:35:23.878
I want to meet her.

00:35:23.955 --> 00:35:25.115
Take a number.

00:35:25.189 --> 00:35:26.156
That was lovely.

00:35:26.224 --> 00:35:27.191
Thank you.

00:35:27.258 --> 00:35:29.692
I've got to admit it...
you've done wonders.

00:35:29.760 --> 00:35:30.852
All right, you win.

00:35:30.928 --> 00:35:32.327
"Win"?

00:35:32.396 --> 00:35:33.590
I know when I'm licked.

00:35:33.664 --> 00:35:35.655
You tell me when you want me
to start those double shifts.

00:35:35.733 --> 00:35:37.598
You made a wager regarding me?

00:35:37.668 --> 00:35:38.600
Clarify.

00:35:38.669 --> 00:35:40.193
It's not what you think.

00:35:40.271 --> 00:35:42.171
Um, don't blame him.

00:35:42.240 --> 00:35:43.673
It was my idea.

00:35:43.741 --> 00:35:45.208
I believed your interest

00:35:45.276 --> 00:35:47.540
in my social
development was sincere,

00:35:47.612 --> 00:35:48.943
not motivated by personal gain.

00:35:49.013 --> 00:35:50.480
It was sincere.

00:35:50.548 --> 00:35:54.348
Clearly, I am not the only one
who requires social lessons.

00:35:54.418 --> 00:35:57.478
Thank you for a lovely evening.

00:36:01.359 --> 00:36:02.690
Hey...

00:36:02.760 --> 00:36:06.321
Why don't we
go back to my quarters?

00:36:06.397 --> 00:36:08.558
I've studied human
mating rituals.

00:36:08.633 --> 00:36:13.002
Remove your hand
or I will remove your arm.

00:36:16.941 --> 00:36:19.842
Did you hear
what she said to me?!

00:36:19.911 --> 00:36:21.538
I am the guest of honor!

00:36:21.612 --> 00:36:23.273
Ambassador,
it's been a long day.

00:36:23.347 --> 00:36:24.905
Maybe you should get some rest.

00:36:24.982 --> 00:36:27.678
No! I'm not leaving!

00:36:27.752 --> 00:36:30.687
I want another drink!

00:36:41.432 --> 00:36:42.865
I thought synthehol
wasn't supposed

00:36:42.934 --> 00:36:44.162
to have this effect on people.

00:36:44.235 --> 00:36:45.293
Most people.

00:36:45.369 --> 00:36:47.200
The enzymes
that break down synthehol

00:36:47.271 --> 00:36:49.034
aren't present
in his bloodstream.

00:36:49.106 --> 00:36:50.698
Can you counteract
the effects?

00:36:50.775 --> 00:36:53.209
I can synthesize the enzymes,
but that'll take days.

00:36:53.277 --> 00:36:55.541
Days? The Captain will
be back in the morning.

00:36:55.613 --> 00:36:57.478
Maybe he needs a cold shower.

00:36:57.548 --> 00:36:59.243
If his superiors
find him like this,

00:36:59.317 --> 00:37:00.909
he'll be banished
from the colony

00:37:00.985 --> 00:37:03.681
and our trade agreement
will go right out the airlock.

00:37:03.754 --> 00:37:05.517
Oh, Seven of mine.

00:37:05.590 --> 00:37:08.457
It may be possible to encode
some of my nanoprobes

00:37:08.526 --> 00:37:10.323
to assimilate
the synthehol molecules.

00:37:10.394 --> 00:37:11.452
Assimilate me.

00:37:11.529 --> 00:37:13.690
There may be
some adverse effects.

00:37:13.764 --> 00:37:14.856
Please...

00:37:14.932 --> 00:37:16.399
But it's worth a try.

00:37:16.467 --> 00:37:17.900
The Kadi have rules against

00:37:17.969 --> 00:37:20.267
medical procedures
that haven't been sanctified.

00:37:20.338 --> 00:37:22.329
I'd say he's already
violated a few rules.

00:37:22.406 --> 00:37:23.498
What's one more?

00:37:23.574 --> 00:37:25.906
Either we treat him
or he remains intoxicated.

00:37:26.010 --> 00:37:27.568
You're his caretaker...
decide.

00:37:29.680 --> 00:37:30.840
Nanoprobes.

00:37:38.589 --> 00:37:40.580
I owe you an apology.

00:37:40.658 --> 00:37:43.149
Nanoprobe extraction is an
insignificant procedure.

00:37:43.227 --> 00:37:44.319
My systems will adapt.

00:37:44.395 --> 00:37:47.489
No... I'm referring
to the... wager I made

00:37:47.565 --> 00:37:48.930
with Ensign Paris.

00:37:49.066 --> 00:37:52.661
I can see how you
might have felt manipulated,

00:37:52.737 --> 00:37:56.366
but I assure you
that was never my intention.

00:37:56.440 --> 00:37:59.932
I accept your apology.

00:38:00.044 --> 00:38:01.875
I want to make this
perfectly clear,

00:38:01.946 --> 00:38:04.039
so there's no room
for misunderstanding.

00:38:04.115 --> 00:38:06.379
I asked you to go with me
to the reception

00:38:06.450 --> 00:38:09.715
because I enjoy your company.

00:38:09.787 --> 00:38:13.154
In fact,
over the last few days,

00:38:13.224 --> 00:38:16.057
I feel as though we've...

00:38:16.127 --> 00:38:18.561
grown closer.

00:38:18.629 --> 00:38:20.358
Closer?

00:38:20.431 --> 00:38:23.059
We've become
more than colleagues.

00:38:23.134 --> 00:38:26.695
We're...

00:38:26.771 --> 00:38:27.897
friends.

00:38:27.972 --> 00:38:29.701
Friends? Agreed.

00:38:29.774 --> 00:38:31.901
I should begin.

00:38:31.976 --> 00:38:34.604
Of course.

00:38:41.118 --> 00:38:42.983
I'll take over from here.

00:38:44.422 --> 00:38:45.354
Mr. Paris...

00:38:45.423 --> 00:38:47.254
hypothetically...

00:38:47.325 --> 00:38:49.759
if one develops romantic
feelings for another person,

00:38:49.827 --> 00:38:52.557
how does one usually
go about expressing them?

00:38:52.630 --> 00:38:54.928
It's for one of Seven's
social lessons.

00:38:55.032 --> 00:38:58.468
Ah... well, I recommend
the direct approach.

00:38:58.536 --> 00:39:00.800
Tell the person how you feel.

00:39:00.871 --> 00:39:03.237
What if the feelings
aren't mutual?

00:39:03.307 --> 00:39:06.640
Well, that's the risk
you always take.

00:39:06.711 --> 00:39:08.338
Oh... thank you.

00:39:13.050 --> 00:39:14.881
Why don't you tell her?

00:39:15.019 --> 00:39:16.816
Come on, Doc.

00:39:16.887 --> 00:39:18.081
It's obvious the Ambassador

00:39:18.155 --> 00:39:20.487
is not the only one
in this room who's intoxicated.

00:39:20.558 --> 00:39:21.718
Impossible.

00:39:21.792 --> 00:39:23.657
She's my student.

00:39:23.728 --> 00:39:25.525
A hologram and a Borg?

00:39:25.596 --> 00:39:28.121
Stranger things have happened.

00:39:28.199 --> 00:39:30.224
Just look at me and B'Elanna.

00:39:37.341 --> 00:39:40.139
Uh, could... could we
walk a little slower?

00:39:40.211 --> 00:39:42.338
They're due back any minute.

00:39:42.413 --> 00:39:44.677
But my throat feels
like an ancient parchment.

00:39:44.749 --> 00:39:47.582
Can't we go back to Sandrine's
for a refreshing glass of...

00:39:47.651 --> 00:39:49.175
Oh, no, no, no, no.

00:39:49.253 --> 00:39:50.845
No. No, no, no, no.

00:39:50.921 --> 00:39:53.321
Those doors... they're so loud.

00:39:53.391 --> 00:39:55.916
You've got a hangover.

00:39:55.993 --> 00:39:58.928
Neelix, I don't remember
much of last night,

00:39:58.996 --> 00:40:01.362
but... I imagine I might
have said some things...

00:40:01.432 --> 00:40:02.490
You spoke eloquently...

00:40:02.566 --> 00:40:03.498
charmed the entire crew...

00:40:03.567 --> 00:40:06.502
your reception was a success.
Understand?

00:40:06.570 --> 00:40:07.502
Yes.

00:40:07.571 --> 00:40:09.732
Neelix, you've been
most patient.

00:40:09.807 --> 00:40:11.206
Well, that's my job.

00:40:11.275 --> 00:40:13.470
And it isn't over yet.

00:40:17.114 --> 00:40:18.138
Welcome back!

00:40:18.215 --> 00:40:19.477
Good to be home.

00:40:19.550 --> 00:40:20.482
How's it going?

00:40:20.551 --> 00:40:22.280
All systems
functioning normally.

00:40:22.353 --> 00:40:24.378
Ensign Kim detected
a minor fluctuation

00:40:24.455 --> 00:40:26.821
in the sensor array,
but he took care of it.

00:40:26.891 --> 00:40:28.483
I was referring
to Ambassador Tomin.

00:40:28.559 --> 00:40:29.583
Did he enjoy his visit?

00:40:29.660 --> 00:40:30.627
Oh, well...

00:40:30.694 --> 00:40:33.254
well, I would say that he, uh...

00:40:33.330 --> 00:40:34.957
he enjoyed himself immensely.

00:40:35.099 --> 00:40:38.330
There are many distractions
aboard this vessel.

00:40:38.402 --> 00:40:41.337
You didn't indulge
in any of their more...

00:40:41.405 --> 00:40:43.236
colorful traditions?

00:40:43.307 --> 00:40:44.968
Of course not!

00:40:45.042 --> 00:40:47.476
We followed the itinerary
that you approved

00:40:47.545 --> 00:40:48.671
to the last detail.

00:40:48.746 --> 00:40:50.407
Oh... shame.

00:40:50.481 --> 00:40:51.914
Your Holiness?

00:40:51.982 --> 00:40:56.282
It isn't a violation
to explore new experiences...

00:40:56.353 --> 00:40:58.844
as long as you don't make
a habit of it.

00:40:58.923 --> 00:41:01.118
I see your point.

00:41:01.192 --> 00:41:03.786
Shall we conclude
our negotiations, Captain?

00:41:03.861 --> 00:41:04.919
By all means.

00:41:05.029 --> 00:41:06.462
I'll show you
to the briefing room.

00:41:06.530 --> 00:41:08.157
Good work... Ambassador.

00:41:20.978 --> 00:41:23.708
Do you like them?

00:41:23.781 --> 00:41:25.442
Species Rosa rubifolia.

00:41:31.021 --> 00:41:32.249
State your intention.

00:41:32.323 --> 00:41:33.950
I wanted to congratulate you

00:41:34.058 --> 00:41:36.652
on the latest phase
of your social development.

00:41:36.727 --> 00:41:39.389
Why don't you read the card?

00:41:43.868 --> 00:41:45.563
"You are my sunshine."

00:41:48.038 --> 00:41:52.839
These past few days have been...

00:41:52.910 --> 00:41:54.343
unforgettable.

00:41:54.411 --> 00:41:57.642
You've brought light
into my life, Seven.

00:41:59.350 --> 00:42:01.841
You have developed
romantic feelings for me.

00:42:01.919 --> 00:42:04.114
It's as if you've become
a part of my program.

00:42:04.188 --> 00:42:05.655
When we're apart,

00:42:05.723 --> 00:42:08.920
I feel like
I'm missing a subroutine.

00:42:09.059 --> 00:42:12.392
I don't expect you
to reciprocate...

00:42:12.463 --> 00:42:17.423
but I wanted you
to know how I feel.

00:42:18.869 --> 00:42:22.032
Computer, end program.

00:42:23.374 --> 00:42:24.466
Enter.

00:42:27.411 --> 00:42:28.935
Seven...

00:42:29.079 --> 00:42:30.341
I wish to speak with you.

00:42:30.414 --> 00:42:31.506
What a coincidence.

00:42:31.582 --> 00:42:35.484
I... was hoping to speak
with you as well.

00:42:35.553 --> 00:42:36.986
Regarding?

00:42:38.589 --> 00:42:39.886
You first.

00:42:45.563 --> 00:42:46.655
What's this?

00:42:46.730 --> 00:42:48.664
It's a medical tricorder.

00:42:48.732 --> 00:42:51.326
I enhanced its scanning
resolution by 33 percent.

00:42:51.402 --> 00:42:54.894
You once stated you desired
a more efficient instrument.

00:42:54.972 --> 00:42:58.066
I suppose I did.

00:42:58.142 --> 00:42:59.609
It is a gift.

00:42:59.677 --> 00:43:02.373
Lesson 22..."Thanks
for the Memories."

00:43:05.215 --> 00:43:06.273
Is it insufficient?

00:43:06.350 --> 00:43:08.910
No... no.

00:43:09.053 --> 00:43:11.749
It's very thoughtful.

00:43:11.822 --> 00:43:13.346
I chose to convey my gratitude
at this time

00:43:13.424 --> 00:43:15.051
because I no longer require
your assistance.

00:43:15.125 --> 00:43:16.752
It's obvious there are

00:43:16.827 --> 00:43:18.920
no potential mates for me
aboard this vessel.

00:43:19.063 --> 00:43:20.928
However, if I encounter
a compatible individual

00:43:21.031 --> 00:43:22.999
in the future, I will again
seek your guidance.

00:43:25.603 --> 00:43:27.332
Guidance.

00:43:28.372 --> 00:43:29.566
Of course.

00:43:29.640 --> 00:43:32.234
You said you had something
to tell me.

00:43:34.945 --> 00:43:38.881
I just wanted to say...

00:43:38.949 --> 00:43:43.852
the past few days...

00:43:43.921 --> 00:43:46.685
have been unforgettable.

00:43:46.757 --> 00:43:48.122
Thank you.

00:43:48.192 --> 00:43:50.854
You're welcome.

00:43:58.002 --> 00:44:02.632
